From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: expose read-only MII control in link snapshot

The IPQ5332 SGMII physical receiver can report carrier while GMAC sees
zero frames after the copper PHY first links late. Add a bounded raw
MII control readback, including force-mode and adapter reset bits,
beside the already captured PCS status. Do not alter configuration,
register writes, timing-sensitive callbacks or link-state handling.

Signed-off-by: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -1338,6 +1338,14 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < PCS_MAX_MII_NRS; i++) {
 		if (!qpcs->qpcs_mii[i])
 			continue;
+		ret = regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_CTRL(i), &val);
+		if (ret)
+			seq_printf(s, "mii%d_control error=%d\n", i, ret);
+		else
+			seq_printf(s,
+				   "mii%d_control=0x%08x force=%u adapter_reset=%u\n",
+				   i, val, !!(val & PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE),
+				   !!(val & PCS_MII_ADPT_RESET));
 		ret = regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_STS(i), &val);
 		if (ret)
 			seq_printf(s, "mii%d_status error=%d\n", i, ret);
